00:06:25,714 --> 00:06:31,714
The Thirteenth Tale is a tv movie, drama, mystery film directed by James Kent.

2
00:12:51,428 --> 00:12:57,428
Biographer Margaret Lea travels to the isolated rural mansion of the famous
writer Vida Winter, who asks her to write her biography.

3
00:19:17,142 --> 00:19:23,142
Although initially she is reluctant, as Vida is known for constantly distorting the facts of her life, Margaret soon becomes fascinated
with the story of a dark childhood, a disturbing tale that leads her to finally confront the traumas of her own past.

4
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
Vida Winter, played by Vanessa Redgrave.

5
00:32:08,571 --> 00:32:14,571
Margaret, played by Olivia Colman.

6
00:38:34,285 --> 00:38:40,285
John the Dig, played by Robert Pugh.

7
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Hester Barrow, played by Alexandra Roach.

8
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Dr. Clifton, played by Steven Mackintosh.

9
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
Dr. Mawsley, played by Tom Goodman-Hill.

10
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The Thirteenth Tale is a British drama television film that
first broadcast on BBC Two on 30 December 2013.

11
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
It is an adaptation of Diane Setterfield's 2006
gothic novel The Thirteenth Tale.

12
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
The film explores themes of countryside, based on novel or book, family
secrets, isolated house, brother sister relationship.

13
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
The tone is mind_bending and dark and emotional.
